codex
The root cause is now concrete: processes see namespace PIDs (for example PID 3), while this sandbox’s `/proc` mount lacks `/proc/3/exe`; Lean 4.22 resolves its own executable via `/proc/<getpid()>/exe`, so both Lake and Lean fail before checking code. I’m applying a narrow audit-local compatibility shim that maps only `/proc/<digits>/exe` reads to the equivalent `/proc/self/exe`, then I’ll rerun the unchanged trusted preflight checker.
apply patch
